{"id":"hydrocodone","name":"Hydrocodone","form":"tablet","status":"Well-documented","aliases":"vicodin, hydro","category":"Opioid","chemicalClass":"Substituted morphinans","psychoactiveClass":"Opioids","addictionPotential":"moderately addictive","toxicity":["potentially fatal at heavy dosages"],"summarySources":"PsychonautWiki, TripSit","summary":"A codeine-derived opioid generally unheard of outside the United States. Reported to be weaker in subjective effects, the drug is used as an analgesic, cough-suppresant, and recreationally.","advisory":"Avoid: Alcohol due to CNS depression. Grapefruit juice, which inhibits enzymes that leads to increased abosrbtion rate, risking possible overdose.","doseMaxTick":60,"doseUnit":"mg","doseRows":[{"roa":"Oral","source":"PsychonautWiki","unit":"mg","threshold":"3 mg","light":"5–10 mg","common":"10–25 mg","strong":"25–40 mg","heavy":"40 mg+","commonEstimate":18,"band":{"low":10,"high":25},"domain":[2.4,55],"segments":{"light":[5,10],"common":[10,25],"strong":[25,40],"heavy":[40,52.8]},"absorbed":{"min":70,"max":70,"source":"Wikipedia","page":"Hydrocodone"}}],"durationSources":"PsychonautWiki, TripSit","durationRows":[{"roa":"Oral","onset":"10–60 min","comeup":"—","peak":"—","offset":"—","afterEffects":"—","total":"4–8 h"}],"tolerance":{"buildUp":"with prolonged use","reset":"1 - 2 weeks","milestones":[{"label":"Full tolerance","value":"with prolonged use","tone":"danger"},{"label":"Half tolerance","value":"3 - 7 days","tone":"warning"},{"label":"Baseline","value":"1 - 2 weeks","tone":"positive"}],"crossTolerances":[{"group":"Cross-tolerance","items":["Opioids"]}]},"subjectiveEffects":[{"name":"Anxiety suppression","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Anxiety_suppression"},{"name":"Cognitive euphoria","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Cognitive_euphoria"},{"name":"Compulsive redosing","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Compulsive_redosing"},{"name":"Constipation","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Constipation"},{"name":"Cough suppression","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Cough_suppression"},{"name":"Difficulty urinating","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Difficulty_urinating"},{"name":"Itchiness","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Itchiness"},{"name":"Pain relief","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Pain_relief"},{"name":"Physical euphoria","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Physical_euphoria"},{"name":"Pupil constriction","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Pupil_constriction"},{"name":"Respiratory depression","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Respiratory_depression"},{"name":"Sedation","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Sedation"},{"name":"Euphoria"},{"name":"Dry Mouth"},{"name":"Mood lift"},{"name":"Relaxant"},{"name":"Analgesia"}],"combinations":[{"substance":"Alcohol","status":"Dangerous","tone":"danger","note":"Documented dangerous interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Benzodiazepines","status":"Dangerous","tone":"danger","note":"Documented dangerous interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Dxm","status":"Dangerous","tone":"danger","note":"Documented dangerous interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Gbl","status":"Dangerous","tone":"danger","note":"Documented dangerous interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Ghb","status":"Dangerous","tone":"danger","note":"Documented dangerous interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Grapefruit","status":"Dangerous","tone":"danger","note":"Documented dangerous interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Ketamine","status":"Dangerous","tone":"danger","note":"Documented dangerous interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"MXE","status":"Dangerous","tone":"danger","note":"Documented dangerous interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Tramadol","status":"Dangerous","tone":"danger","note":"Documented dangerous interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"MAOIs","status":"Caution","tone":"warning","note":"Uncertain or unpredictable interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Nitrous","status":"Caution","tone":"warning","note":"Uncertain or unpredictable interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"PCP","status":"Caution","tone":"warning","note":"Uncertain or unpredictable interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Stimulants","status":"Caution","tone":"warning","note":"Uncertain or unpredictable interaction on PsychonautWiki."}],"citations":[],"helpfulLinks":[{"title":"PsychonautWiki","description":"Pharmacology, subjective effects, and dosage reference","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Hydrocodone"},{"title":"TripSit Factsheet","description":"Rapid harm-reduction summary and combination data","url":"https://drugs.tripsit.me/hydrocodone"},{"title":"Erowid Experience Vaults","description":"First-person experience reports and archives","url":"https://www.erowid.org/experiences/subs/exp_Hydrocodone.shtml"},{"title":"Wikipedia","description":"Encyclopedia article","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hydrocodone"},{"title":"Wikidata","description":"Structured data on Hydrocodone","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q411441"}],"wikidata":"Q411441","formula":"C18H21NO3","molarMass":299.4,"pharmacology":{"text":"Hydrocodone is a highly selective full agonist of the μ-opioid receptor (MOR). This is the main biological target of the endogenous opioid neuropeptide β-endorphin. Hydrocodone has low affinity for the δ-opioid receptor (DOR) and the κ-opioid receptor (KOR), where it is an agonist similarly.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"Hydrocodone","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hydrocodone#Pharmacodynamics","acts":[{"how":"agonist","on":["κ-opioid receptor","μ-opioid receptor"]}],"guide":7081,"kind":"Opioid","body":[{"what":"halfLife","says":"Average: 3.8 hours; Range: 3.3–4.4 hours"},{"what":"brokenDown","says":"Liver: CYP3A4 (major), CYP2D6 (minor)"},{"what":"turnsInto","says":"Norhydrocodone; Hydromorphone; Others"},{"what":"leaves","says":"Urine"}],"figures":"Hydrocodone"},"uses":{"text":"Hydrocodone is used to treat moderate to severe pain. In liquid formulations, it is used to treat coughing. In one study comparing the potency of hydrocodone to that of oxycodone, it was found that it took 50% more hydrocodone to achieve the same degree of miosis (pupillary contraction). The investigators interpreted this to mean that oxycodone is about 50% more potent than hydrocodone.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"Hydrocodone","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hydrocodone#Medical_uses","brands":"Hysingla ER, Zohydro ER","routes":"Clinical: By mouth; Others: Intranasal, rectal","figures":"Hydrocodone"},"sideEffects":{"text":"Common side effects include dizziness, sleepiness, nausea, and constipation. Serious side effects may include low blood pressure, seizures, QT prolongation, respiratory depression, and serotonin syndrome.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"Hydrocodone","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hydrocodone"}}